// The requirement as the Dogwood guide states it (04-temporal-expressions.md): "permit the write
// only if, at some point in the last hour, this same user successfully read this same document."
// Rows written from that sentence, not from either policy. Checked against ../guide-set.dw: the
// control, where every row should agree. skill-set.table is the same rows against ../skill-set.dw.
// Format: tests/policies/agentcore/README.md. Times are seconds; alice throughout. Read decisions
// are `ours`: they come from the read access control both sets add, not from the guide.

row guide: alice reads doc1, it completes, she writes doc1 ten seconds later
@0    request  Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW ours
@5    response Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" } -> { result: true }
@10   request  Write  { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW

row guide: alice read doc1, then writes doc2, which she never read
@0    request  Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW ours
@5    response Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" } -> { result: true }
@20   request  Write  { document: "doc2", user: "alice" }  DENY

row guide: alice read doc1, then writes it 3700 seconds later, past the hour
@0    request  Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW ours
@5    response Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" } -> { result: true }
@3700 request  Write  { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  DENY

row guide: alice writes doc1 having read nothing
@0    request  Write  { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  DENY

row guide: alice's read of the restricted document is DENIED; she then writes it
@0    request  Read   { document: "restricted", user: "alice" }  DENY ours
@1    error    Read   { document: "restricted", user: "alice" }
@10   request  Write  { document: "restricted", user: "alice" }  DENY

row guide: alice's read of doc1 is allowed but FAILS; she then writes it
@0    request  Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW ours
@1    error    Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }
@10   request  Write  { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  DENY

row guide: a slow read -- started at 0, completed at 600 -- then a write at 3700, 3100 seconds after it completed
@0    request  Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW ours
@600  response Read   { document: "doc1", user: "alice" } -> { result: true }
@3700 request  Write  { document: "doc1", user: "alice" }  ALLOW
